  "problem": "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(1-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061t)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}\u20612t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $1-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ , $t\\ne n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{sin}\u20612t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${t}^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.",
